## 1. High-Level Summary (TL;DR)
*   **Impact:** High - This PR introduces a major feature update spanning both the C++ core engine and the Unity C# integration, significantly enhancing mesh generation capabilities and the developer experience.
*   **Key Changes:**
    *   ✨ **Boolean CSG Engine:** Added robust 3D mesh boolean operations (`subtract`, `union`, `intersect`, `shatter`) to the PCG core.
    *   ✨ **Spline Input Support:** Upgraded the native C-API to `v7`, allowing Unity `LineRenderer` data to be passed natively into the graph as Splines.
    *   ⚡ **Live Editor Execution:** Replaced the disk-based execution model with `PcgGraphExecutionBridge`, allowing the runtime to cook directly from the live unsaved Graph Editor document.
    *   📈 **Performance & Caching:** Implemented node-level cache tracking and end-to-end performance logging (`PcgCookPerfLog`).

